    <p style="text-align:justify;">During arthroscopic surgery, a small camera (arthroscope) is inserted into the joint through tiny incisions. This allows the surgeon to visualize the joint and accurately diagnose conditions such as torn cartilage, ligament injuries, joint inflammation, and other problems. Surgical tools can also be inserted through the same incisions to remove damaged tissue, repair ligaments, or clean the joint. This precise technique reduces pain and accelerates recovery.</p>

